  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Xenon hexafluoride on partial hydrolysis produces compounds&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>​&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8203;</mo></math>. In the compounds,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub></math>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>​, the oxidation states of Xe are&nbsp;+6&nbsp;and&nbsp;+6&nbsp;respectively.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeF</mi><mn>6</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8203;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&#8203;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>HF</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>XeOF</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8203;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8594;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>XeO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msub><mo>&#8203;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>HF</mi></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fd2ec8f0-0ac6-4f94-ab16-e117a10cd1c2-image.png\" style=\"width: 400px; height: 184px;\" /></p>",
